    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
    "body": "### Problem\n\n`zqN` / `zq#` should add a multicursor at matches before the cursor position (with `nowrapscan` on)\n\nI'm not sure if this is intentional given there's [tests for it](https://github.com/neovim/neovim/blob/80ae7e336f97e169bb3d3e7172998a65336472a1/test/functional/editor/mcursor_spec.lua#L378-L388), but the behaviour being the same as `zqn` / `zq*` feels odd\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\nBuffer:\n```\nabc\nxyz abc\nabc\n```\n\n```vim\nset nowrapscan\n```\n\n`2gg$zq*` yields cursors here, as expected:\n```\nabc\nxyz |abc\n|abc\n```\n\nwhereas `2gg$zq#` also yields cursors as above, whereas I would expect:\n```\n|abc\nxyz |abc\nabc\n```\n\n### Expected behavior\n\nCursors should be placed in the direction of the search (when `nowrapscan` is on)\n\n### Nvim version (nvim -v)\n\n0.13.0 commit 80ae7e33\n\n### Vim (not Nvim) behaves the same?\n\nn/a\n\n### Operating system/version\n\nmacOS 27.0.1\n\n### Terminal name/version\n\nalacritty 0.15.1\n\n### $TERM environment variable\n\nxterm-256color\n\n### Installation\n\nbuild from repo",
